  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1246 PM MDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nLatest model data continues to support a cooling and wetting trend\nacross all of south central and southeast Colorado through the end \nof week and into the weekend, as the upper high slides into Southern\nHigh Plains, as an upper trough develops across the West Coast. This\nset up is a classic monsoonal pattern for Colorado, with abundant\nmoisture embedded within modest southwest flow aloft through the \nweekend. The available moisture, combined with upslope flow across\nthe plains behind a passing front across the plains on Thursday, \nwill bring temperatures back down to at and even slightly below \nseasonal levels through the weekend, with expected daily rounds of\nshowers and thunderstorms. We will likely need to issue flash \nflood watches for area burn scars for Thursday, and additional \nflood products for burn scars and other areas into the weekend, \ndepending on coverage of heavy rain and how saturated soils may \nbecome. Those living in and near the recent burn areas should \nremain weather through the weekend. \n\nInto early next week, models support the upper high building back\nacross the Southern Rockies, leading to slight warming within more \nwesterly flow across the region. However, models continue to support\nample moisture within the westerly flow, for continued good coverage\nof daily showers and storms areawide into early next week.",
